---
import Base from '@layouts/Base.astro';
import Hero from '@components/Hero.astro';
import { site, offers, cta } from '@config/site';
import '../styles/home-v10.css';
import '../styles/home-final.css';
import '../styles/intro-v10.css';
---
<Base title={site.name} description={site.description} path="/">
  <Hero />

  <main class="home-v10">
    <section class="proofbar-v10" id="proof" aria-label="Evidence Axis operating principles">
      <div class="container-wide proofbar-v10__grid">
        <article><span>01</span><b>Discover</b><p>Find the competitors that actually matter.</p></article>
        <article><span>02</span><b>Verify</b><p>Separate evidence from marketing noise.</p></article>
        <article><span>03</span><b>Decide</b><p>Turn verified intelligence into a decision.</p></article>
        <article><span>04</span><b>Respond</b><p>Translate the decision into market action.</p></article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="gallery-v10" aria-labelledby="sample-title">
      <div class="container-wide gallery-v10__grid">
        <div class="gallery-v10__copy">
          <span class="v10-kicker">ILLUSTRATIVE SAMPLE</span>
          <h2 id="sample-title">Inspect the intelligence before you discuss an engagement.</h2>
          <p>The public demonstration compares Intercom and Zendesk on a bounded competitive question using checked first-party public sources. It shows the evidence matrix, Fact / Inference / Unknown discipline, decision implications and source register. It is a demonstration, not a client engagement.</p>
          <div class="gallery-v10__links">
            <a href="/sample-report/">View the Sample Intelligence Brief →</a>
            <a href={cta.primary.href}>Discuss a Competitive Decision →</a>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="gallery-v10__mosaic">
          <figure><img src="/assets/v10/approved/market-intelligence-war-room.webp" alt="Evidence Axis competitive intelligence view showing market signals, sources and decisions" loading="eager" /></figure>
          <figure><img src="/assets/v10/approved/two-competitor-decision-brief.webp" alt="Evidence Axis source-verified competitive intelligence brief" loading="lazy" /></figure>
          <figure><img src="/assets/v10/approved/what-you-get.webp" alt="Evidence Axis executive intelligence deliverable with fact, inference and unknown separation" loading="lazy" /></figure>
          <figure><img src="/assets/v10/approved/decision-ready-showcase.webp" alt="Decision-ready competitive intelligence with traceable evidence" loading="lazy" /></figure>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="offers-v10 gift-v10" id="intelligence-gift" aria-labelledby="gift-title">
      <div class="container-wide">
        <header class="offers-v10__head">
          <div>
            <span class="v10-kicker">WE SOMETIMES DO THE WORK FIRST</span>
            <h2 id="gift-title">Selected companies receive intelligence before they ask for it.</h2>
          </div>
          <p>Evidence Axis does not use the Intelligence Gift as a lead magnet or public free-service queue. We select a company because a competitive trigger is visible, build the work, and deliver it directly. No signup, form or call is required to receive it.</p>
        </header>

        <div class="pricing-v10 gift-v10__grid">
          <article class="price-card price-card--cyan gift-v10__card">
            <div class="price-card__flag mono">INVITATION ONLY</div>
            <span class="price-card__label mono">PROACTIVE COMPETITIVE INTELLIGENCE</span>
            <h3>{offers.intelligenceGift.name}</h3>
            <p>{offers.intelligenceGift.scope}</p>
            <div class="price-card__price"><small>ACCESS</small><strong>Selected companies</strong><em>Built before an engagement is requested.</em></div>
            <div class="price-card__delivery"><small>DELIVERY</small><b>{offers.intelligenceGift.delivery}</b></div>
            <ul>
              <li>Competitive Set Scan</li>
              <li>Executive Intelligence Deck — PDF</li>
              <li>Evidence Appendix — PDF</li>
              <li>Fact / Inference / Unknown separation</li>
              <li>Source Register with review dates</li>
              <li>Competitive blindspots where evidence supports them</li>
            </ul>
            <a href="/sample-report/">See the public demonstration →</a>
          </article>

          <aside class="included-card">
            <span class="price-card__label mono">WHY THIS MODEL EXISTS</span>
            <div><b>Quality before persuasion</b><p>The first meaningful interaction can be the work itself, not a sales deck.</p></div>
            <div><b>Trigger-led selection</b><p>We look for an observable competitive change that makes the intelligence timely.</p></div>
            <div><b>Discovery first</b><p>We do not assume the competitors already on a team’s radar are the whole market.</p></div>
            <div><b>Human-reviewed evidence</b><p>Material claims are checked against underlying sources before they enter the deliverable.</p></div>
            <a href="/method/">See the Evidence Axis method →</a>
          </aside>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="insight-v10" aria-labelledby="method-title">
      <div class="container-wide">
        <header class="v10-head v10-head--center">
          <span class="v10-kicker">THE EVIDENCE STANDARD</span>
          <h2 id="method-title">A conclusion is only as strong as the path behind it.</h2>
          <p>Fast summaries are easy. Evidence Axis keeps the source, evidence state, decision boundary and unresolved questions visible so confidence does not outrun the record.</p>
        </header>
        <div class="insight-v10__grid">
          <article class="insight-card insight-card--cyan"><span>01</span><h3>Discovery comes before analysis.</h3><p>A supplied competitor list is useful context, not a guarantee that the competitive set is complete.</p><a href="/method/">See the method →</a></article>
          <article class="insight-card insight-card--blue"><span>02</span><h3>Evidence before interpretation.</h3><p>Material factual claims stay attached to identifiable, checked sources and review dates.</p><a href="/sample-report/">Open the sample →</a></article>
          <article class="insight-card insight-card--amber"><span>03</span><h3>Fact. Inference. Unknown.</h3><p>Verified observations, analytical judgment and unresolved gaps are never silently blended together.</p><a href="/method/#evidence-states">See the evidence states →</a></article>
          <article class="insight-card insight-card--violet"><span>04</span><h3>Contradictions stay visible.</h3><p>Conflicting sources are disclosed rather than resolved by picking the cleaner-looking number.</p><a href="/method/#limitations">See the boundaries →</a></article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="ai-v10" aria-labelledby="ai-title">
      <div class="container-wide ai-v10__grid">
        <div class="ai-v10__copy">
          <span class="v10-kicker v10-kicker--light">AI-ACCELERATED · EVIDENCE-CONTROLLED</span>
          <h2 id="ai-title">AI can accelerate the search. It does not get to decide what is true.</h2>
          <p>Evidence Axis uses AI where it creates leverage — discovery, organization, comparison and pattern-finding. Material claims still have to survive the evidence standard before they reach an executive deliverable.</p>
          <ul class="ai-v10__points">
            <li>Underlying sources are opened and checked before material claims are used.</li>
            <li>Search snippets, generated summaries and vendor comparison pages are not treated as neutral proof.</li>
            <li>Fact, Inference, Unknown and contradictions stay visibly separate.</li>
            <li>AI makes the workflow faster; human review controls what enters the decision.</li>
          </ul>
          <a class="v10-link v10-link--light" href="/method/">See the evidence workflow →</a>
        </div>
        <figure class="ai-v10__visual">
          <img src="/assets/v10/approved/what-you-get.webp" alt="Evidence Axis evidence-controlled intelligence workflow with source verification and executive outputs" loading="lazy" />
        </figure>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="offers-v10" id="services" aria-labelledby="services-title">
      <div class="container-wide">
        <header class="offers-v10__head">
          <div><span class="v10-kicker">PAID ENGAGEMENTS</span><h2 id="services-title">When the evidence raises a real decision, go deeper.</h2></div>
          <p>The paid engagement is not simply a longer brief. It combines verified market evidence with your internal context, the decision requirement and the response options available to your team.</p>
        </header>

        <div class="pricing-v10">
          <article class="price-card price-card--cyan">
            <div class="price-card__flag mono">PAID CORE</div>
            <span class="price-card__label mono">DECIDE</span>
            <h3>{offers.decisionSprint.name}</h3>
            <p>{offers.decisionSprint.scope}</p>
            <div class="price-card__price"><small>ENGAGEMENT</small><strong>{offers.decisionSprint.priceDisplay}</strong></div>
            <div class="price-card__delivery"><small>DELIVERY</small><b>{offers.decisionSprint.delivery}</b></div>
            <ul><li>Decision context and constraints</li><li>Decision-critical competitor deep dive</li><li>Pricing / product / positioning implications</li><li>Prioritized recommendations</li><li>Executive Decision Deck + Evidence Appendix</li></ul>
            <a href="/competitor-brief/">Explore the Decision Sprint →</a>
          </article>

          <article class="price-card price-card--orange">
            <div class="price-card__flag mono">ACT</div>
            <span class="price-card__label mono">RESPOND</span>
            <h3>{offers.responseSprint.name}</h3>
            <p>{offers.responseSprint.scope}</p>
            <div class="price-card__price"><small>ENGAGEMENT</small><strong>{offers.responseSprint.priceDisplay}</strong></div>
            <div class="price-card__delivery"><small>DELIVERY</small><b>{offers.responseSprint.delivery}</b></div>
            <ul><li>Competitive battlecards</li><li>Objection handling</li><li>Pricing response</li><li>Positioning and messaging response</li><li>Competitor-specific enablement</li></ul>
            <a href="/strategic-blueprint/">Explore the Response Sprint →</a>
          </article>

          <article class="price-card price-card--violet">
            <div class="price-card__flag mono">ONGOING</div>
            <span class="price-card__label mono">MONITOR</span>
            <h3>{offers.radar.name}</h3>
            <p>{offers.radar.scope}</p>
            <div class="price-card__price"><small>ENGAGEMENT</small><strong>{offers.radar.priceDisplay}</strong></div>
            <div class="price-card__delivery"><small>CADENCE</small><b>{offers.radar.delivery}</b></div>
            <ul><li>Pricing and packaging changes</li><li>Launches and feature moves</li><li>Positioning shifts</li><li>Funding, expansion and integrations</li><li>New or emerging competitors</li></ul>
            <a href="/market-intelligence/">Explore Competitive Radar →</a>
          </article>

          <aside class="included-card">
            <span class="price-card__label mono">THE BOUNDARY</span>
            <div><b>The Intelligence Gift proves capability.</b><p>For selected companies, it reveals and verifies the public competitive landscape before an engagement exists.</p></div>
            <div><b>The Decision Sprint adds your context.</b><p>It answers what the evidence means for the decision actually in front of your team.</p></div>
            <div><b>The Response Sprint builds the response.</b><p>It converts the decision into the assets needed to act.</p></div>
            <div><b>Radar keeps it current.</b><p>Monitoring matters when the competitive picture changes faster than a point-in-time brief.</p></div>
            <a href={cta.primary.href}>Discuss a Competitive Decision →</a>
          </aside>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="deliverables-v10" id="what-you-get" aria-labelledby="deliverables-title">
      <div class="container-wide">
        <header class="deliverables-v10__head">
          <div><span class="v10-kicker">WHAT THE WORK CONTAINS</span><h2 id="deliverables-title">Decision-ready intelligence, with the evidence behind it.</h2></div>
          <p>Every engagement is bounded to the decision. The competitive set, evidence depth and response work change with the question; the evidence standard does not.</p>
        </header>
        <div class="deliverables-v10__grid">
          <article><span>01</span><small>DISCOVERY</small><h3>Competitive Set Scan.</h3><p>We identify and verify candidates rather than assuming the market begins and ends with the names already known internally.</p></article>
          <article><span>02</span><small>DEEP DIVE</small><h3>The competitors that matter.</h3><p>Product, pricing, positioning, public claims and recent moves are investigated where they are decision-relevant.</p></article>
          <article><span>03</span><small>CLASSIFICATION</small><h3>Fact. Inference. Unknown.</h3><p>What is verified stays separate from analytical judgment and unresolved gaps.</p></article>
          <article><span>04</span><small>EXECUTIVE OUTPUT</small><h3>Executive Decision Deck.</h3><p>A concise PDF built for senior review, with a decision matrix and implications rather than raw research volume.</p></article>
          <article><span>05</span><small>EVIDENCE OUTPUT</small><h3>Evidence Appendix.</h3><p>The detailed support behind the executive deck: source URLs, source classes, review dates, limitations and contradictions.</p></article>
          <article><span>06</span><small>THE RESULT</small><h3>A stronger decision.</h3><p>What the evidence supports, what remains uncertain, what may be outside your radar and what deserves action next.</p></article>
        </div>
        <div class="deliverables-v10__bottom"><b>Independent competitive intelligence</b><span>Public evidence · client context where applicable · executive-ready output</span><a href={cta.primary.href}>Discuss a Competitive Decision →</a></div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="film-v10" id="system-film" data-surface="dark" aria-labelledby="film-title">
      <div class="container-wide film-v10__grid">
        <div class="film-v10__copy">
          <span class="v10-kicker v10-kicker--light">RESEARCH SYSTEM</span>
          <h2 id="film-title">See the evidence system behind the brief.</h2>
          <p>This visual tour shows how signals, sources, evidence states and decision views connect. The client-facing deliverables remain the Executive Decision Deck and Evidence Appendix.</p>
          <div class="film-v10__chips mono"><span>DISCOVERY</span><span>EVIDENCE</span><span>DECISION</span><span>SOURCE TRAIL</span></div>
        </div>
        <div class="film-v10__stage film-v10__stage--real-video">
          <div class="film-v10__player film-v10__player--real-video" aria-label="Evidence Axis research system film">
            <video class="film-v10__video" autoplay muted loop playsinline preload="metadata" poster="/assets/evidence-axis/product-tour-poster.jpg" aria-label="Evidence Axis research system — evidence matrix, decision view and source workflow">
              <source src="/assets/evidence-axis/product-tour.mp4" type="video/mp4" />
            </video>
            <div class="film-v10__frame"><span>RESEARCH SYSTEM</span><b>Discovery · evidence · decision · source trail</b></div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="offers-v10 close-v10" aria-labelledby="close-title">
      <div class="container-wide close-v10__inner">
        <span class="v10-kicker">A REAL COMPETITIVE DECISION</span>
        <h2 id="close-title">Bring the question. We will define the evidence boundary.</h2>
        <p>Send the decision context asynchronously. If Evidence Axis is a fit, scope, delivery and price are confirmed in writing before paid work begins.</p>
        <div class="close-v10__actions"><a class="btn btn--lg" href={cta.primary.href}>Discuss a Competitive Decision <span class="btn-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a href="/sample-report/">Inspect the sample first →</a></div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <style>
    .gift-v10{background:linear-gradient(180deg,#f7f9fc,#eef4f8)}
    .gift-v10__grid{grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1.1fr) minmax(18rem,.9fr)}
    .gift-v10__card .price-card__price strong{font-size:clamp(1.9rem,3vw,3rem)}
    .close-v10{background:#f8f4ed}
    .close-v10__inner{max-width:72rem}
    .close-v10 h2{max-width:14ch;margin:.7rem 0 1rem;font-size:clamp(2.8rem,5vw,5rem);line-height:.95;letter-spacing:-.05em}
    .close-v10 p{max-width:50rem;color:var(--text-muted);font-size:1.08rem;line-height:1.7}
    .close-v10__actions{display:flex;align-items:center;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:1rem;margin-top:1.5rem}.close-v10__actions>a:not(.btn){font-family:var(--font-display);font-weight:750;text-decoration:none}
    @media(max-width:920px){.gift-v10__grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}}
  </style>
</Base>
